# fixedbugs, defect 151, lane land186, 2026-10-02 (panel 186 R3), the
# critic's `one_arm_union` under the one rule.
#
# A union TYPE is held to the rule a union inside a struct is: compared by an
# integer arm, the arm must be as wide as the union, which C can name here,
# so the width is `sizeof(UB)`. `b` is one byte of eight.

extern "fixedbugs-151-unions.h"
    record UB  #~ ffi_union_field
        b: i8

function same(x: UB, y: UB) -> bool
    return x == y

function main()
    print(1)
